# UI Patterns

## Dashboard

- **Structure:** Page title and subtitle, then a grid of KPI cards, then a "Quick Actions" section with buttons linking to machine-failure alerts, analysis, reports, settings (match Angular dashboard links).
- **KPI cards:** Machines Online (online/total, percentage, status class), Active Alerts (total, critical/warning breakdown), Failure Rate (current %, trend vs previous period), OEE (overall + availability/performance/quality breakdown). Use Tailwind for status classes (e.g. excellent/good/warning/critical based on percentage).
- **Loading:** Show a loading overlay or skeleton while KPIs are loading (e.g. `loading.tsx` or inline loading state). Do not render KPI grid until data is ready or show placeholders.
- **Data:** Load KPI data in a Server Component or via a data layer; avoid using `useEffect` for initial fetch when server fetch is possible.

## Machine Failure Section

- **Tabs:** Tab strip for Overview, Alerts, Analysis, AI Insights. Drive tabs from the same nav config as the sidebar (e.g. machine-failure children). Use Next.js `<Link>` with `usePathname()` for active tab styling.
- **Overview page:** Header with title and last-updated; Failed Products block (see below); KPI cards for failure KPIs; 7-day failure trends (chart or placeholder); Top Failure Causes (Pareto-style list with rank, cause, category, occurrences, percentage, avg downtime, progress bar). Match Angular overview structure.
- **Failed Products block:** Table/chart of failed products; filters for severity and status (all/critical/high/…); loading state; error state with message and retry button; empty state ("No failed products found"). Use centralized error messages and types from the data layer.
- **Alerts / Analysis / AI Insights:** Rebuild content to match Angular placeholders; use consistent layout (header, content area) and loading/error patterns.

## Loading, Error, and Empty States

- **Loading:** Use a single pattern: spinner, skeleton, or "Loading…" text. Prefer `loading.tsx` for route-level loading where applicable.
- **Error:** Show user-facing message from central error config; for server/network/unknown errors show a retry button. Use the same error type → message mapping as in the data layer.
- **Empty:** When the API returns 200 but empty data (e.g. no failed products), show a friendly empty message, not an error style.

## Charts

- **Library:** Use one charting library (e.g. Recharts or Tremor) for the app. Do not mix multiple chart libs. Replace Angular ngx-charts with the chosen library.
- **Data shape:** Transform API data (e.g. `FailedProductDto.failedProductCount`) into the chart library's expected format (e.g. `{ name, value }[]` per series). Keep transformation logic in a single place (component or util).

## General

- Use semantic HTML (section, header, main, nav) and Tailwind for layout and styling.
- Keep interactive elements (buttons, links) accessible (focus, labels). Prefer composition of small components over one large page component.
